From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:46:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: a stream whose delivery fails ends at once in the base
 scheduler, TF_GLM_DELIVERY_ABORT (MiaAI-Lab recipe patch 0083)

In TensorFold's base scheduler (cuda/scheduler.py), a delivery callback that raised (a broken pipe, a reset, a
timeout) left submit with the exception while the stream decoded on into a queue nobody read, holding its lane until
generation ended. MiaAI-Lab's recipe v1.8 ends such a stream at once with patch 0083-tfcap-delivery-abort (by
johnwhited, after vLLM v1's generate-abort behaviour): _relay_token latches the cancel on a True return or a failure
and skips later tokens. GLM's GlmScheduler.submit has its own loop and does not change, in the recipe too (its
delivery failures are recipe patch 0073's, TF_GLM_QUEUED_CANCEL in this tree); on the AFD split the switch is
therefore inert for GLM, and the CUDA server's on_tokens never raises into either loop (it keeps a failure and raises
it after generate returns). Ported for the base scheduler's other users (TensorFold's other CUDA families), behind a
switch of this tree's own, off by default:

- cuda/scheduler.py: delivery_abort() reads TF_GLM_DELIVERY_ABORT when a Scheduler starts (0 or unset: off, 1: on,
  anything else refused); _relay_token verbatim (its except Exception with a noqa comment); submit relays through it
  when the switch is on, else as before.
- engine.py: a startup line when the switch is on, saying GLM's own loop is unchanged.
- THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md: "Delivery abort in the base scheduler".

Unset, submit relays as before.

Tests (CPU): tests/test_cuda_delivery_abort.py (9): the switch's values; unset, a failing delivery leaves submit and the
stream decodes all its tokens; on, submit returns, the stream ends within a round or two and its lane serves the next
request, and the failure is logged; a client that leaves (True) ends the stream either way; a reply served whole is
unchanged either way; GlmScheduler keeps its own loop with the switch set; the relay fires once and latches.

Credit: patch 0083 was written by johnwhited (https://github.com/johnwhited) in
MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold pull request #48 (commits 2eaf324, 9d2fd5e), with vLLM v1's
generate-abort behaviour as its reference; MiaAI-Lab applied it as contributed (merge 0cbe026, renumbered in e6bc3e0,
v1.8 at 33b50fd), Apache License 2.0.

