+generate-abort behaviour (Apache 2.0) as its reference. Under the recipe's Apache License 2.0 (see
+[the license text](LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)). Changes in the port: the recipe always relays through `_relay_token`, and
+here `submit` does only with `TF_GLM_DELIVERY_ABORT=1` (`delivery_abort`, read when the scheduler starts; unset or 0:
+the relay as before); its `except Exception` carries a `noqa` comment. GLM's `GlmScheduler.submit` has its own loop,
+which this does not change, in the recipe too (GLM's delivery failures are recipe patch 0073's,
+`TF_GLM_QUEUED_CANCEL`).
